    <!-- ==================== Tolerance page ==================== -->
    <string name="tolerance_title">Food Tolerance</string>
    <string name="tolerance_subtitle">Track which foods you can eat and which to be careful with; tag foods when logging meals for easy review</string>
    <string name="tolerance_note_title">About tolerance</string>
    <string name="tolerance_note">Food tolerance varies from person to person depending on physical condition and disease state. Currently, no specific food has been clearly shown to cause inflammation. During active disease, you must eat a light, low-residue diet and take small, frequent meals to reduce the burden on your intestines. After the disease has settled into remission, you can start testing food tolerance. Add small amounts at a time; if there is no problem after two or three days, you can basically consider it tolerable. Even so, you should still maintain a cautious, healthy eating style, avoid irritating foods, and promote intestinal health.</string>
